Package: bridges
Title: Fit, Detect, and Visualize Breakage-Fusion-Bridge in Single-Cell Copy Number Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Giovanni", "Santacatterina", , "first.last@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Simulates single-cell copy-number evolution under a
    continuous-time Gillespie process (bridge_sim()), including
    breakage-fusion-bridge (BFB) cycles, focal amplifications/deletions,
    and whole-genome duplication; infers phylogenies from single-cell
    copy-number data (fit()); detects BFB signal both on inferred tree
    branches (detect_bfb_branches()) and directly on raw per-cell
    profiles via exact BFB combinatorics (bfb_detect_batch()); and
    visualizes the results as annotated heatmaps. Depends on 'bfbtools'
    for the underlying linear-time BFB count-vector algorithms, kept as
    a separate package because it is GPL-3 licensed (a derivative of
    GPL-3 reference code), unlike this package (MIT).
License: MIT + file LICENSE
